message: "If you use this software or its coded data, please cite it as below."
title: "world-impact: usage is not necessity -- two instruments for scientific importance, and a landscape tool built on the result"
abstract: >-
  Two instruments for measuring the importance of scientific work, and the measurement
  that shows they disagree. A bibliometric instrument over 520 works (the twenty
  most-cited in each of 26 fields, ten criteria, consensus across criteria) returns a
  top twelve that is entirely instrumentation -- software, assays, datasets and
  reporting standards. A dependency instrument over 150 coded results, ranked by
  transitive reach, returns the infinitesimal calculus, induction, Carnot, entropy,
  Maxwell, Planck and the Turing machine. The two top-twelve lists share zero entries.
  Citation count is in-degree (use); importance is transitive in-degree (necessity); a
  citation edge is untyped, so no refinement of a bibliometric ranking recovers the
  distinction. Also ships a landscape tool that applies both columns to a narrowed
  focus -- a seed paper or a topic -- and leads with the works a field structurally
  depends on and does not cite directly.
